WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
London, 1831.

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.330
Cholera arrived, bringing
with it fear and panic.

3
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:09.890
In summer 1858 came the Great Stink.

4
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.710
Many blamed miasma, a
poisonous vapour in the air.

5
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:18.270
Then Charles Booth coloured every street
by the income and social class of its

6
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:19.770
inhabitants.

7
00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:23.290
Poverty was mapped, and
fear was attached to place.

8
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:28.370
So why do so many young adults now choose
to live in the city Victorians feared?

9
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.250
In this mission, you'll see how
a perception is built from data,

10
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.730
the media and lived experience.

11
00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.950
Then you'll compare an
inner borough with a suburb,

12
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.190
using census data.

13
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:43.890
Your mission: explain why so many young
adults now choose to live in London.
